25,2,1,talk,Minato,,"Chasing money for individual sessions takes way too much time. Also, calculating part-year fees for new joiners is a real headache.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
26,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,"Most of our costs are fixed, like insurance and hall hire. Also, many people struggle to pay the full renewal fee at once.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
27,2,1,talk,Minako,,"Past tiered systems caused friction and discouraged lower grades. Plus, some potential members are scared off by a large upfront annual commitment.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
28,2,1,talk,May,,Turnout for weekday meetings dropped after we added charges to summer outings. Some members also feel uneasy about the cost per visit.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
29,2,1,talk,Shunichi,,"A tiny group of people attend almost everything and do all the setup work, while many others barely show up at all.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
30,2,2,talk,Minato,,"@Ryuji, if people struggle with one big payment, maybe we should change how we collect it?","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
31,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Minato, but the treasurer's workload is already high. We can't make the collection process more complex.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
32,2,2,talk,Minako,,"@May, it sounds like any ""pay-as-you-go"" feel might actually discourage people from coming to the regular sessions.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
33,2,2,talk,May,,"@Minako, that's exactly it. But some people feel it's unfair to pay for things they don't use.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
34,2,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Ryuji, if the costs are mostly fixed, then the people who attend every day are essentially subsidizing the ghosts.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
35,2,3,talk,Minato,,I just don't want the next treasurer to quit because they're spending every evening on paperwork.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,We need a system that covers the fixed costs without relying on guesswork or constant chasing.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,3,talk,Minako,,"We have to be careful. If we make the tiers too obvious, we might lose the inclusive feel of the club.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,3,talk,May,,"If we make it too expensive to join, we'll lose the taster crowd and the casuals.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,3,talk,Shunichi,,The current imbalance is unsustainable. The regulars are doing all the work and paying the same as the absentees.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
