50,3,1,talk,Minato,,"Option A is the easiest for the treasurer, but Option B seems like a nightmare for the paperwork.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,3,1,talk,Ryuji,,"Option A ensures the fixed costs are covered, but the bank statements show people struggle with one large sum.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,3,1,talk,Minako,,Option C reminds me of the friction in the old minute books. I'm wary of tiered levels.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,3,1,talk,May,,"Option B might make people hesitate to attend weekday meetings, which we already saw happen in the summer.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,3,1,talk,Shunichi,,"Option A is unfair to the regulars. Option B is fairer, but Option C could reward the high-users.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
55,3,2,talk,Minato,,"@Shunichi, would Option B really be fairer if it means the treasurer spends six hours a month chasing coins?","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
56,3,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Minato, that's a huge point. Option B is a logistical disaster for the staff.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
57,3,2,talk,Minako,,"@May, if Option A is too much at once, maybe we can't do it, but Option C creates a social divide.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
58,3,2,talk,May,,"@Ryuji, if we go with Option A, will we lose the people who can't pay upfront?","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
59,3,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Minato, I agree the workload is a problem. Maybe Option C is a middle ground for fairness and effort.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
60,3,3,talk,Minato,,I'm leaning toward Option A. It's the only way to save the treasurer's sanity.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,3,talk,Ryuji,,I agree. Option A is the most stable for the budget and the least risky for the account.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,3,talk,Minako,,I'll vote for Option A. It avoids the social friction of tiers and the instability of activity fees.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,3,talk,May,,"I'm worried about the cost barrier, but Option B is too discouraging for attendance. I'll go with A.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,3,talk,Shunichi,,"I still hate the unfairness, but if B is a paperwork nightmare and C is socially divisive, A is the only choice.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,4,talk,Minato,,I vote A.,"{""words"":3,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
